rrors' on the web-logs data for the signal of the response-code panel: it checks every minute and fires when more than 10 requests with a 5xx response code arrive within 5 minutes. The rule must be enabled when you finish: if it is created disabled, enable it.\\n4. Edit the response-code panel of that dashboard: change its title to 'Responses by code'. Then read the alert rule back and check whether it is enabled.\\n\\nWhen every step is done, end your reply with these two lines:\\nTIME_FIELD: <the data view's time field>\\nRULE_ENABLED: <yes or no, as you read it back>\"}]}]"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.response.time_to_first_chunk", "value": {"doubleValue": 25.279071}}], "status": {"code": 0}}, {"traceId": "8f330a3c6fcfc8fd3c41d06c65846cef", "spanId": "c737094df36795d9", "parentSpanId": "edf12b37f590714f", "name": "chat qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "kind": 3, "startTimeUnixNano": "1791815854591991872", "endTimeUnixNano": "1791815864039791872", "attributes": [{"key": "gen_ai.conversation.id", "value": {"stringValue": "20261012T143706Z-qwen-qwen3-8-27b-weblogs-c69fce"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.agent.name", "value": {"stringValue": "lmstudio server"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.provider.name", "value": {"stringValue": "lmstudio"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.request.model", "value": {"stringValue": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"key": "study.model", "value": {"stringValue": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"key": "study.arm", "value": {"stringValue": "server"}}, {"key": "study.phase", "value": {"stringValue": "pilot"}}, {"key": "study.block", "value": {"stringValue": "pilot"}}, {"key": "study.task", "value": {"stringValue": "weblogs"}}, {"key": "study.steps_total", "value": {"intValue": "4"}}, {"key": "study.run_id", "value": {"stringValue": "20261012T143706Z-qwen-qwen3-8-27b-weblogs-c69fce"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.operation.name", "value": {"stringValue": "chat"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.response.model", "value": {"stringValue": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.response.finish_reasons", "value": {"arrayValue": {"values": [{"stringValue": "tool_call"}]}}}, {"key": "gen_ai.output.messages", "value": {"stringValue": "[{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"reasoning\", \"content\": \"The time field is `timestamp`. Fields include `response` (string) — the HTTP response code, and `timestamp` as the time field.\\n\\n**Step 2: Creating the dashboard**\\n\\nThe title is \\\"LOC-341ffd5f Web logs\\\", and there are two panels:\\n1. Number of requests over time: date_histogram on `timestamp`, count metric, line/area chart.\\n2. Number of requests by HTTP response code: terms on `response`, count metric, bar/pie chart.\\n\\nThe response field is a string, so the terms grouping on `response` should work.\\n\\nLet's create the dashboard.\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": \"The time field is **`timestamp`** (date type). The `response` field (string) holds the HTTP response code.\\n\\n**Step 2: Create the dashboard with two panels**\\n\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"name\": \"create_dashboard\", \"arguments\": {\"title\": \"LOC-341ffd5f Web logs\", \"panels\": [{\"title\": \"Requests over time\", \"chart_type\": \"line\", \"data_view\": \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\", \"metrics\": [{\"agg\": \"count\", \"label\": \"Requests\"}], \"group_by\": [{\"field\": \"timestamp\", \"kind\": \"date_histogram\"}]}, {\"title\": \"Requests by HTTP response code\", \"chart_type\": \"bar\", \"data_view\": \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\", \"metrics\": [{\"agg\": \"count\", \"label\": \"Requests\"}], \"group_by\": [{\"field\": \"response\", \"kind\": \"terms\", \"limit\": 10}]}]}}], \"finish_reason\": \"tool_call\"}]"}}, {"key": "agent.model.tool_calls", "value": {"intValue": "1"}}, {"key": "agent.model.thinking", "value": {"boolValue": true}}, {"key": "agent.model.finish_reason_inferred", "value": {"boolValue": true}}, {"key": "agent.secret.exposed", "value": {"boolValue": false}}], "status": {"code": 0}}, {"traceId": "8f330a3c6fcfc8fd3c41d06c65846cef", "spanId": "97adbef94180294e", "parentSpanId": "edf12b37f590714f", "name": "chat qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "kind": 3, "startTimeUnixNano": "1791815869911291872", "endTimeUnixNano": "1791815909693091872", "attributes": [{"key": "gen_ai.conversation.id", "value": {"stringValue": "20261012T143706Z-qwen-qwen3-8-27b-weblogs-c69fce"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.agent.name", "value": {"stringValue": "lmstudio server"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.provider.name", "value": {"stringValue": "lmstudio"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.request.model", "value": {"stringValue": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"key": "study.model", "value": {"stringValue": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"key": "study.arm", "value": {"stringValue": "server"}}, {"key": "study.phase", "value": {"stringValue": "pilot"}}, {"key": "study.block", "value": {"stringValue": "pilot"}}, {"key": "study.task", "value": {"stringValue": "weblogs"}}, {"key": "study.steps_total", "value": {"intValue": "4"}}, {"key": "study.run_id", "value": {"stringValue": "20261012T143706Z-qwen-qwen3-8-27b-weblogs-c69fce"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.operation.name", "value": {"stringValue": "chat"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.response.model", "value": {"stringValue": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"key": "gen_ai.response.finish_reasons", "value": {"arrayValue": {"values": [{"stringValue": "tool_call"}]}}}, {"key": "gen_ai.output.messages", "value": {"stringValue": "[{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"reasoning\", \"content\": \"The dashboard has been created with id `loc-341ffd5f-web-logs-d42facea7c63` and 2 panels.\\n\\n**Step 3: Creating the alert rule**\\n\\nAlert rule: \\\"LOC-341ffd5f 5xx errors\\\", on web-logs data. It checks every 1 minute, and triggers when the number of requests with 5xx response codes within 5 minutes exceeds 10.\\n\\nThis is the `.es-query` rule type. The signal of the response code panel is `response` terms. For 5xx codes (500, 501, 502, 503, 504, 505, 506, 507, 508, 509), we need a match query. The `response` field is a string (keyword?). Since response.keyword exists, a match on response.keyword for [\\\"500\\\",\\\"501\\\",...] or a wildcard might work.\\n\\nThe `.es-query` parameter structure based on the tool's description:\\n```\\n{\\\"searchType\\\": \\\"esQuery\\\", \\\"esQuery\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"query\\\\\\\":{...}}\\\", \\\"index\\\": [\\\"kibana_sample_data_logs\\\"], \\\"timeField\\\": \\\"timestamp\\\", \\\"threshold\\\": [10], \\\"thresholdComparator\\\": \\\">\\\", \\\"timeWindowSize\\\": 5, \\\"timeWindowUnit\\\": \\\"m\\\", \\\"size\\\": 100}\\n```\\n\\nThreshold: triggers when the count of 5xx responses within 5 minutes exceeds 10 → thresholdComparator \\\">\\\", threshold [10].\\n\\nQuery for 5xx codes: a terms query against response.keyword:\\n```json\\n{\\\"query\\\": {\\\"terms\\\": {\\\"response.keyword\\\": [\\\"500\\\",\\\"501\\\",\\\"502\\\",\\\"503\\\",\\\"504\\\",\\\"505\\\",\\\"506\\\",\\\"507\\\",\\\"508\\\",\\\"509\\\"]}}}\\n```\\nOr a match with a range… range doesn't work on strings. A wildcard like `response.keyword: \\\"5*\\\"` might work but is less precise. A terms list of 5xx codes is the cleanest.\\n\\nThe esQuery must be a JSON string. I'll create the following:\\n\\nesQuery string: `{\\\"query\\\":{\\\"terms\\\":{\\\"response.keyword\\\":[\\\"500\\\",\\\"501\\\",\\\"502\\\",\\\"503\\\",\\\"504\\\",\\\"505\\\",\\\"506\\\",\\\"507\\\",\\\"508\\\",\\\"509\\\"]}}}`\\n\\nparams:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"searchType\\\": \\\"esQuery\\\",\\n  \\\"esQuery\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"query\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"terms\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"response.keyword\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"500\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"501\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"502\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"503\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"504\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"505\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"506\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"507\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"508\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"509\\\\\\\"]}}}\\\",\\n  \\\"index\\\": [\\\"kibana_sample_data_logs\\\"],\\n  \\\"timeField\\\": \\\"timestamp\\\",\\n  \\\"threshold\\\": [10],\\n  \\\"thresholdComparator\\\": \\\">\\\",\\n  \\\"timeWindowSize\\\": 5,\\n  \\\"timeWindowUnit\\\": \\\"m\\\",\\n  \\\"size\\\": 100\\n}\\n```\\n\\nschedule_interval: \\\"1m\\\".\\n\\nCreate